---
description: Payment, role, and inventory validation instructions for local coding agents
alwaysApply: true
---
When editing checkout, test with deterministic mock and actual PayPal sandbox separately. Never call mock payment a PayPal transaction.
Use `PayPal-Request-Id` on every eligible modifying request. Do not retry uncertain captures with new IDs. Read provider order status.
When editing stock, test conditional reservation with simultaneous buyers and expiry. An internal demo hold is not a POS hold.
Every merchant-sensitive endpoint requires server-side authorization; never use `x-demo-role` outside localhost DEMO_MODE.
Run `cd apps/api && PYTHONPATH=. pytest -q` after every backend change and `cd apps/web && npm run build` after UI edits once deps installed.
AG Studio and Metronic have nontrivial licenses; do not publish licensed source without explicit permissions.
For integrations, preserve data-source provenance, branch identity and consent: online offers are NOT physically local inventory.
